    "body": "This affects the thread sanitizer test that we run in free-threaded mode. It ends up re-enabling the GIL without this flag (because we don't mark extension modules as freethreading-compatible)\r\n\r\nFor the other tests, it get gets set conditionally in ci-run.sh depending on the value of `PYTHON_VERSION`. Just setting it unconditionally seems easier to me than fighting with GitHub actions to make it conditional. In GIL builds the environment variable will just be ignored so it's harmless.",
