                },
                "message": "Set PYTHON_GIL=0 in sanitizers tests \n\nThis affects the thread sanitizer test that we run in free-threaded mode. It ends up re-enabling the GIL without this flag (because we don't mark extension modules as freethreading-compatible)\r\n\r\nFor the other tests, it get gets set conditionally in ci-run.sh depending on the value of `PYTHON_VERSION`. Just setting it unconditionally seems easier to me than fighting with GitHub actions to make it conditional. In GIL builds the environment variable will just be ignored so it's harmless.",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "f6f63fcac70b1197a33602d5e7cfc33b2118f944",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/trees/f6f63fcac70b1197a33602d5e7cfc33b2118f944"
                },
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/commits/c950f7b9a652ad7235bf5547cccd79ad538d3617",
                "verification": {
                    "payload": "tree f6f63fcac70b1197a33602d5e7cfc33b2118f944\nparent dbbbdbb97f116c46495b5ab88ba0195a277016f9\nauthor da-woods <dw-git@d-woods.co.uk> 1789321350 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789321350 +0100\n\nSet PYTHON_GIL=0 in sanitizers tests \n\nThis affects the thread sanitizer test that we run in free-threaded mode. It ends up re-enabling the GIL without this flag (because we don't mark extension modules as freethreading-compatible)\r\n\r\nFor the other tests, it get gets set conditionally in ci-run.sh depending on the value of `PYTHON_VERSION`. Just setting it unconditionally seems easier to me than fighting with GitHub actions to make it conditional. In GIL builds the environment variable will just be ignored so it's harmless.",
